   "image": "port/bateau_pirate.jpg",
   "alt": "The main deck of a life-size wooden pirate ship moored in the harbor's glass-roofed boat shed on a family dress-up day; there are no swords or cannons. High in the crow's nest at the upper left a person in a giant carrot costume keeps a lookout with cupped hands. A laughing pirate holds up his boot with a brass compass stuck to the sole. At the front left two dress-up children gaze at a shiny red toy car on a stack of cargo crates and sacks, and a sailor kneels at an open deck hatch, calling down into the dark hold. In the middle a helmsman in a tricorn hat steers at the big wooden wheel, and a smiling mother in a headscarf hugs the tall mast. On the raised deck at the right a dashing privateer in a plumed hat points out ahead, and two mischievous bandits grin and wave from the ship's little barred brig. A pirate kid opens a loot sack full of giant colorful buttons, a girl blows soap bubbles out of a round brass porthole, and a little rat in a red bandana sits on a barrel holding one big green pea. Door: the open doorway at the top of the gangway on the left, back out to the sunny harbor quay.",
